WEBVTT

00:07.591 --> 00:09.800
It's pretty cool
we got our own mural, huh?

00:09.801 --> 00:10.968
Eh, don't get too excited.

00:10.969 --> 00:12.386
You know who else has one?

00:12.387 --> 00:15.264
- The Ox-Bow Incident.
- What is that?

00:15.265 --> 00:18.976
Set in Bridger's Wells, Nevada in 1885,

00:18.977 --> 00:23.189
The Ox-Bow Incident is a tale
of cowboys, cattle and conflict.

00:23.190 --> 00:26.025
<i>If you guys could just take a seat.</i>

00:26.026 --> 00:28.486
<i>Okay, here we go.</i>

00:31.430 --> 00:36.494
<i>Okay, welcome to Family Guy
DVD commentary for episode 1614.</i>

00:36.495 --> 00:38.829
<i>I'm Peter Griffin,
joined by my wife Lois,</i>

00:38.830 --> 00:40.039
<i>our dog Brian,</i>

00:40.040 --> 00:42.375
<i>and our children, Meg, Stewie and Chris.</i>

00:42.376 --> 00:44.919
<i>And for you kids out
there, DVDs were plastic discs...</i>

00:44.920 --> 00:46.254
<i>I-I got this, Brian.</i>

00:46.255 --> 00:47.797
<i>Have you ever been
at your grandmother's house</i>

00:47.798 --> 00:50.341
<i>and you look at her weird, old computer,</i>

00:50.342 --> 00:52.218
<i>and there's, like,
a crack on the side of it?</i>

00:52.219 --> 00:54.095
<i>That's DVDs.</i>

00:54.096 --> 00:56.347
<i>Oh, and animation producer
Shannon Smith is here, too.</i>

00:56.348 --> 00:58.224
<i>Glad to be here. This is actually...</i>

00:58.225 --> 00:59.559
<i>Oh, wait, wait. Look, look.</i>

00:59.560 --> 01:01.060
<i>Lot of people don't know this,</i>

01:01.061 --> 01:03.062
<i>but that house is actually in Burbank.</i>

01:03.063 --> 01:04.981
<i>People keep stealing their mailbox.</i>

01:04.982 --> 01:06.075
<i>We now return to</i>

01:06.076 --> 01:09.277
<i>"Winona Ryder Distracting from
Other Speeches in History."</i>

01:09.278 --> 01:11.279
<i>Four score and seven years ago...</i>

01:11.280 --> 01:13.155
<i>Wow, yeah, yeah, I remember this.</i>

01:13.156 --> 01:15.866
<i>Winona Ryder kind of hung out
on set all day,</i>

01:15.867 --> 01:18.244
<i>and it, uh, wore a little thin
on all of us.</i>

01:18.245 --> 01:19.662
<i>Yeah, I actually had to</i>

01:19.663 --> 01:21.247
<i>close a door on her at one point.</i>

01:21.248 --> 01:22.665
<i>I-I just remember she stole</i>

01:22.666 --> 01:24.625
<i>a ton of LUNA Bars
from the office kitchen.</i>

01:24.626 --> 01:26.085
<i>Like-like, filled a whole duffel bag.</i>

01:26.086 --> 01:27.587
Great news, everyone.

01:27.588 --> 01:29.630
The new smartphone
from Crabapple is out.

01:29.631 --> 01:32.240
The new Crabapple phone? Awesome!

01:32.241 --> 01:33.634
Yeah, the network doesn't like us using

01:33.635 --> 01:35.469
the names of actual companies
on the show.

01:35.470 --> 01:36.929
<i>It's not so bad, though.</i>

01:36.930 --> 01:40.433
<i>We can still say Burger Kong,
McDarrel's, Kooka Cola,</i>

01:40.434 --> 01:43.269
<i>Pipsi, Chevrolump and all the big ones.</i>

01:43.270 --> 01:45.646
I want to be the first
to get the new phone.

01:45.647 --> 01:47.565
I don't care if it takes all day.

01:47.566 --> 01:48.774
Don't you have work?

01:48.775 --> 01:50.151
Eh, I wouldn't mind missing work.

01:50.152 --> 01:52.111
There's a secretary
looking for reassurance

01:52.112 --> 01:54.072
about her overly short haircut.

01:55.282 --> 01:57.074
I saw it in a magazine.

01:57.075 --> 01:59.255
I needed a fresh start.

01:59.256 --> 02:00.620
Stop pretending to stare at your phones,

02:00.621 --> 02:02.371
and just say you hate it.

02:02.372 --> 02:05.458
Sir, I am trying to read.

02:05.459 --> 02:08.336
<i>Ah, the writer credits have begun.</i>

02:08.337 --> 02:10.046
<i>I'm gonna give personal facts</i>

02:10.047 --> 02:12.048
<i>about each of the names that pops up.</i>

02:12.049 --> 02:13.466
Mom, will you tie my shoes?

02:13.467 --> 02:15.968
<i>Smokes on the no-smoking balcony.</i>

02:15.969 --> 02:18.220
<i>Weird church guy.</i>

02:18.221 --> 02:21.390
<i>Instagrams cowboy hats at 3:00 a.m.</i>

02:21.391 --> 02:23.809
<i>Pushed his wife at a party.</i>

02:23.810 --> 02:25.186
<i>Oh, my God, Cherry's the best.</i>

02:25.187 --> 02:27.146
<i>We love her. Hi, Cherry. We love you.</i>

02:27.147 --> 02:29.565
Kids, time to gather up
our old cords and chargers

02:29.566 --> 02:31.692
that no longer work
and throw them in the garbage.

02:31.693 --> 02:33.027
We can't do that.

02:33.028 --> 02:34.820
Don't you know a lot
of discarded electronics

02:34.821 --> 02:36.864
end up in the ocean
and kill sea turtles?

02:36.865 --> 02:38.699
Well, then let's cut out the middleman.

02:38.700 --> 02:41.035
I'm sorry. There's a new phone.

02:41.036 --> 02:43.788
<i>That was cool.
I got to go to Fiji for that.</i>

02:43.789 --> 02:45.831
<i>They got a ton of turtles there.</i>

02:45.832 --> 02:46.999
<i>You can kill 'em, nobody cares.</i>

02:47.000 --> 02:49.543
<i>Oh my gosh. I just got it.</i>

02:49.544 --> 02:50.961
<i>Crab-apple.</i>

02:50.962 --> 02:52.964
<i>Take a lap, Meg.
Think about what you said.</i>

02:53.965 --> 02:55.716
Hey. Gold phone is mine.

02:55.717 --> 02:57.301
Already match fingernail.

02:57.302 --> 02:59.929
<i>Oh, this is where I fight
that woman for the phone.</i>

02:59.930 --> 03:02.765
I was here first! That's mine!

03:02.766 --> 03:04.975
<i>You know, I actually
had a couple of ad-libs</i>

03:04.976 --> 03:06.435
<i>about Chinese working conditions</i>

03:06.436 --> 03:08.270
<i>that somehow didn't make it
into the final cut.</i>

03:08.271 --> 03:10.690
<i>All you said was,
"Children make iPhones."</i>

03:10.691 --> 03:13.859
<i>This is a comedy show,
not Mark Ruffalo's Twitter.</i>

03:13.860 --> 03:15.695
She wanted it more than me.

03:16.863 --> 03:18.615
<i>Take it easy, huh?</i>

03:21.034 --> 03:23.244
Peter, I'm just not sure
it's such a great idea

03:23.245 --> 03:25.746
that everyone in the family
got a new cell phone.

03:25.747 --> 03:27.790
<i>Is that my bottle of water?</i>

03:27.791 --> 03:29.125
<i>Wh-What?</i>

03:29.126 --> 03:31.836
<i>That open bottle...
Is that yours or mine?</i>

03:31.837 --> 03:34.130
<i>I-I... I don't know. Maybe yours?</i>

03:34.131 --> 03:36.674
<i>This is why we need a Sharpie in here</i>

03:36.675 --> 03:39.176
<i>to put our names on our water!</i>

03:39.177 --> 03:40.594
<i>Geez, Chris. What the hell?</i>

03:40.595 --> 03:42.430
<i>Chris, relax. Have a Pipsi.</i>

03:42.431 --> 03:43.973
Good morning, everybod...

03:43.974 --> 03:45.599
Damn it!

03:45.600 --> 03:48.185
She's just gonna keep it like
that for the next three years.

03:48.186 --> 03:49.228
<i>You know, there's truth to that.</i>

03:49.229 --> 03:51.063
<i>You-you can tell a lot about a person</i>

03:51.064 --> 03:52.064
<i>whose cell phone screen is cracked.</i>

03:52.065 --> 03:53.858
<i>Like-like, if they're a girl,</i>

03:53.859 --> 03:55.568
<i>they definitely celebrate
their birth week.</i>

03:55.569 --> 03:57.361
<i>Oh, yeah. Just trash.</i>

03:57.362 --> 03:59.029
Damn it, those phones have

03:59.030 --> 04:01.073
turned you all into mindless drones.

04:01.074 --> 04:02.658
I knew this would happen.

04:02.659 --> 04:04.577
Getting those things
was a worse idea than...

04:04.578 --> 04:06.704
<i>You know, for an extra $12 a month,</i>

04:06.705 --> 04:09.165
<i>you can insure your screen,
and they'll replace it for free.</i>

04:09.166 --> 04:10.875
<i>Nice going, Meg.</i>

04:10.876 --> 04:12.293
<i>You talked over the setup
of this cutaway,</i>

04:12.294 --> 04:14.128
<i>and now we don't know what's going on.</i>

04:14.129 --> 04:15.463
<i>Looks like Nicki Minaj,</i>

04:15.464 --> 04:18.507
<i>Iggy Azalea and Madonna
are robbing a bank.</i>

04:18.508 --> 04:20.134
<i>Um... they're butt bandits?</i>

04:20.135 --> 04:22.845
<i>"Ocean's 36-24-49?"</i>

04:22.846 --> 04:25.097
<i>Oh, I remember. They're all skanks.</i>

04:25.098 --> 04:27.975
<i>"Getting new phones was a worse
idea than a skank robbery."</i>

04:27.976 --> 04:29.977
<i>- Oh, yeah.
- Right, skank robbery.</i>

04:29.978 --> 04:32.980
<i>I'm sorry, that's not funny.</i>

04:32.981 --> 04:35.775
Today's sermon is about perseverance.

04:35.776 --> 04:38.903
When I was run out of Boston
by the Spotlight team,

04:38.904 --> 04:40.988
I could've hung up my collar.

04:40.989 --> 04:42.281
Oh, my God. Again?

04:42.282 --> 04:44.617
You guys have got to put those away.

04:44.618 --> 04:46.660
You can't be on your phones in here.

04:46.661 --> 04:49.330
Relax, Lois. It's just
stupid, boring church.

04:49.331 --> 04:51.081
Not like we're gonna miss anything.

04:51.082 --> 04:54.001
But instead, I packed my Bibles
and my Tootsie Pops

04:54.002 --> 04:56.086
and headed down to Quahog.

04:56.087 --> 04:59.924
With a renewed sense of spirit
and a renewed reverence for...

04:59.925 --> 05:02.676
Jesus Christ?

05:02.677 --> 05:04.845
<i>Uh, guys, sorry to interrupt.</i>

05:04.846 --> 05:06.639
<i>Danny the intern is here
with your paychecks.</i>

05:06.640 --> 05:08.390
<i>Oh, thanks, Danny.</i>

05:08.391 --> 05:10.059
<i>Hey, Chris, here's your paycheck.</i>

05:10.060 --> 05:12.853
<i>Yeah, that gets
forwarded right to DraftKings.</i>

05:12.854 --> 05:14.063
What's going on in there, Ollie?

05:14.064 --> 05:15.064
- He came back!
- How is he?

05:15.065 --> 05:17.066
- Mad!
- Thanks, Ollie.

05:17.067 --> 05:18.234
<i>H-Hold on, Danny, it looks like</i>

05:18.235 --> 05:20.069
<i>you accidentally gave me Peter's check.</i>

05:20.070 --> 05:22.029
<i>Wait. What the hell?</i>

05:22.030 --> 05:24.412
<i>This number is four times what I make.</i>

05:24.413 --> 05:26.744
<i>Peter, you always said
you made the same as me.</i>

05:27.860 --> 05:28.869
<i>I'm sorry, Lois.</i>

05:28.870 --> 05:30.830
<i>I couldn't hear you
over Meg's Snickers wrapper.</i>

05:30.831 --> 05:32.706
<i>- What's this, now?
- I can't believe this, Peter.</i>

05:32.707 --> 05:34.625
<i>Y-You lied to me.</i>

05:34.626 --> 05:36.794
Let's get out of here, other altar boys.

05:36.795 --> 05:38.087
<i>This is bull crap.</i>

05:38.088 --> 05:41.006
<i>I'm calling Fox
or Disney payroll right now.</i>

05:42.843 --> 05:44.385
<i>Fox or Disney payroll.</i>

05:44.386 --> 05:46.387
<i>- Yeah, hi. This is Lois Griff...
- Please hold.</i>

05:47.889 --> 05:49.431
<i>Of course.</i>

05:49.432 --> 05:51.475
Yeah, Mom, that's not fair.

05:51.476 --> 05:53.686
Meg is right. That's not fair.

05:53.687 --> 05:55.855
<i>Thank you for continuing to hold.</i>

05:55.856 --> 05:57.815
Turn my family into brain-dead robots.

05:57.816 --> 05:59.233
In fact, you know what?

05:59.234 --> 06:01.944
We're finally going
to Old Sturbridge Village.

06:01.945 --> 06:04.196
<i>Thank you for continuing to hold.</i>

06:04.197 --> 06:06.991
See what life was like
before all these screens.

06:06.992 --> 06:09.243
A place where people farm
their own food,

06:09.244 --> 06:11.161
make their own clothing
and read books...

06:11.162 --> 06:12.830
<i>Thank you for continuing to hold.</i>

06:12.831 --> 06:14.707
Oh, come on, Lois, you only want to go

06:14.708 --> 06:16.458
to Old Sturbridge Village
'cause you once got

06:16.459 --> 06:18.294
hand-blasted there on a field trip.

06:18.295 --> 06:19.628
Yes, let's just say the candles

06:19.629 --> 06:21.922
weren't the only thing being hot-dipped.

06:21.923 --> 06:24.049
<i>You see, Brian?
That's how you do an ad-lib.</i>

06:24.050 --> 06:25.134
Went right in.

06:25.135 --> 06:26.719
<i>Thanks for holding.</i>

06:26.720 --> 06:28.262
<i>How may I help you, Mrs. Griffin?</i>

06:28.263 --> 06:30.055
<i>Yeah, I'll tell you how.</i>

06:30.056 --> 06:31.724
<i>You can explain to me why my husband</i>

06:31.725 --> 06:34.018
<i>makes four times as much money as I do.</i>

06:34.019 --> 06:36.270
<i>Oh, um... okay, this is awkward.</i>

06:36.271 --> 06:39.148
<i>But I... I, um... I assumed you knew.</i>

06:39.149 --> 06:42.234
<i>Mr. Griffin was able
to negotiate a higher salary</i>

06:42.235 --> 06:45.112
<i>because he's still paying
alimony to his first wife.</i>

06:45.113 --> 06:46.655
<i>"First wife"? What?</i>

06:46.656 --> 06:49.185
<i>Peter, you were married before?</i>

06:50.118 --> 06:53.037
<i>We actually freelance
all our explosion animation.</i>

06:53.038 --> 06:54.788
<i>Who are you again?</i>

06:54.789 --> 06:57.249
<i>- I-I'm Shannon Smith.
- Shannon. Take a lap.</i>

06:57.250 --> 06:59.483
<i>Never go to church.</i>

07:02.223 --> 07:04.433
How come you never told me
you were married before?

07:04.434 --> 07:06.101
I don't know. Just never came up.

07:06.102 --> 07:08.714
Never came up?! Well, who was she?

07:08.715 --> 07:10.538
<i>- Sarah Paulson.
- Who?</i>

07:10.539 --> 07:12.013
<i>Wait, isn't she that actress</i>

07:12.014 --> 07:13.536
<i>who's always biting her lip?</i>

07:13.537 --> 07:15.042
<i>Her very full lip.</i>

07:15.043 --> 07:18.129
<i>I honestly have no idea
who they're talking about.</i>

07:18.130 --> 07:20.715
<i>Come on, Sarah Paulson's
been in a lot of stuff, Chris.</i>

07:20.716 --> 07:22.258
<i>Okay, pulled her up on my phone.</i>

07:22.259 --> 07:23.843
<i>Looks vaguely familiar.</i>

07:23.844 --> 07:25.595
<i>But I would legitimately suggest</i>

07:25.596 --> 07:27.972
<i>that people pause this right now
and Google her.</i>

07:27.973 --> 07:29.432
<i>Wait. Wasn't Sarah Paulson</i>

07:29.433 --> 07:30.975
<i>a guest star in this exact episode?</i>

07:30.976 --> 07:32.810
<i>Yeah, in fact, she was in this O.J. gag.</i>

07:32.811 --> 07:35.021
<i>Ah, look, Predator
just cut her head off.</i>

07:35.022 --> 07:37.190
<i>Not for real, though.
For real, she's actually</i>

07:37.191 --> 07:39.692
<i>coming into the booth right now
to be part of this commentary.</i>

07:39.693 --> 07:42.445
<i>Hi, everybody. So sorry I'm late.</i>

07:42.446 --> 07:43.946
<i>I was stuck in the canyon.</i>

07:43.947 --> 07:46.365
<i>Is... is that a
euphemism for lesbian sex?</i>

07:46.366 --> 07:48.451
<i>I don't think I've met everyone.
I'm Sarah.</i>

07:48.452 --> 07:51.037
<i>I understand you and
Peter used to be married.</i>

07:51.038 --> 07:52.455
<i>Oh, that.</i>

07:52.456 --> 07:54.373
<i>Feels like ancient history.</i>

07:54.374 --> 07:57.210
<i>I like your shoulder
blades, Miss Paulson.</i>

07:57.211 --> 07:59.170
<i>They're very... jutty.</i>

07:59.171 --> 08:00.379
<i>Have a seat, Sarah.</i>

08:00.380 --> 08:02.089
<i>Shall I explain what we're doing here?</i>

08:02.090 --> 08:03.382
<i>That's okay. It seems just like</i>

08:03.383 --> 08:05.051
<i>when I would do ADR
for American Horror Story,</i>

08:05.052 --> 08:07.887
<i>for which I have received
five Emmy nominations.</i>

08:07.888 --> 08:09.597
<i>Well, some of us have awards,</i>

08:09.598 --> 08:10.848
<i>some of us have children.</i>

08:10.849 --> 08:12.308
<i>What's that supposed to mean?</i>

08:12.309 --> 08:13.684
<i>Well, I don't know.</i>

08:13.685 --> 08:16.604
<i>You're the smart award winner.
You figure it out.</i>

08:16.605 --> 08:19.273
Because this is a godless show.

08:19.274 --> 08:20.525
All right, I'll do it.

08:20.526 --> 08:21.901
I'll pretend to be sick

08:21.902 --> 08:24.278
to get out of going
to Old Sturbridge Village.

08:24.279 --> 08:27.156
Mm, still 126.

08:27.157 --> 08:29.575
Oh, I wish you were feeling
well enough to come.

08:29.576 --> 08:31.661
Maybe I should stay home
and take care of you.

08:31.662 --> 08:32.912
No. Go, Lois.

08:32.913 --> 08:35.540
Go watch dead-eyed
pale women make bread.

08:35.541 --> 08:38.376
<i>So, Lois, what will you be
wearing to the Emmys this year?</i>

08:38.377 --> 08:41.087
<i>I think you know I won't be there.</i>

08:41.088 --> 08:43.256
<i>I won a surfboard
at the Teen Choice Awards.</i>

08:43.257 --> 08:44.841
<i>I left it in the kitchen at work,</i>

08:44.842 --> 08:46.008
<i>hoping someone would take it.</i>

08:46.009 --> 08:47.677
<i>No one did.</i>

08:47.678 --> 08:49.929
Eat a meatball sub
and watch football all day.

08:49.930 --> 08:51.889
Man, this is an even better scam

08:51.890 --> 08:54.016
than Ferris Bueller's Day On.

08:54.017 --> 08:56.018
Okay, I need you to file these

08:56.019 --> 08:58.521
and not be working
with a shampoo Mohawk.

08:58.522 --> 09:02.066
<i>So, Sarah, I-I guess you
chose not to take Peter's name, huh?</i>

09:02.067 --> 09:03.609
<i>Decided to stick with "Paulson"?</i>

09:03.610 --> 09:05.152
<i>Yeah, his name just felt</i>

09:05.153 --> 09:07.989
<i>kind of, I don't know, rough, you know?</i>

09:07.990 --> 09:09.282
<i>"Griffin."</i>

09:09.283 --> 09:10.491
<i>Right?</i>

09:10.492 --> 09:12.910
<i>Just sounds kind of brutish
and low-class.</i>

09:12.911 --> 09:16.289
<i>I also won an Emmy for
my performance as Marcia Clark</i>

09:16.290 --> 09:17.999
<i>in The People vs. O.J. Simpson.</i>

09:18.000 --> 09:20.001
<i>You won an Emmy for wearing a wig.</i>

09:20.002 --> 09:21.794
<i>Peter, may I speak with you outside?</i>

09:21.795 --> 09:23.643
Oh, boy.

09:24.882 --> 09:26.799
Uh-oh. I think I'm stuck.

09:26.800 --> 09:28.259
<i>Oh, right, this is where</i>

09:28.260 --> 09:30.136
<i>the fat man got stuck
in the banister slats.</i>

09:30.137 --> 09:32.346
<i>Stewie, I'm gonna give
you another crack at that,</i>

09:32.347 --> 09:34.348
<i>because I believe
what you meant to call them was</i>

09:34.349 --> 09:36.670
<i>"baluster slats," not "banister slats."</i>

09:36.671 --> 09:38.530
<i>"Banister," "baluster." Same thing.</i>

09:38.531 --> 09:39.725
<i>Stewie,</i>

09:39.726 --> 09:42.899
<i>"banister" and "baluster"
are hardly the same things.</i>

09:42.900 --> 09:46.444
<i>A banister is the handrail that
sits atop the upright supports.</i>

09:46.445 --> 09:49.322
<i>A baluster is the
supporting structure itself.</i>

09:49.323 --> 09:51.866
<i>- Is this my water?
- No, it is not!</i>

09:51.867 --> 09:54.327
<i>Brian, I've heard
people say "banister slats."</i>

09:54.328 --> 09:56.454
<i>Well, those people,
like you, would be incorrect.</i>

09:56.455 --> 09:57.914
<i>So, the baluster is that</i>

09:57.915 --> 09:59.790
<i>big, round thing
at the bottom of the stairs</i>

09:59.791 --> 10:01.959
<i>- where the staircase begins?
- "Big, round thing"?</i>

10:01.960 --> 10:03.961
<i>You're...
you're just guessing stuff now.</i>

10:03.962 --> 10:06.672
<i>I believe what you're
referring to is a newel post.</i>

10:06.673 --> 10:08.925
<i>Mom and Dad are still out there arguing.</i>

10:08.926 --> 10:10.551
<i>Shouldn't they be in here?</i>

10:10.552 --> 10:12.094
<i>I'll get 'em.</i>

10:12.095 --> 10:14.894
<i>Wasn't Shannon, like, a P.A. here once?</i>

10:14.895 --> 10:15.926
<i>Shut your mouth.</i>

10:15.927 --> 10:17.391
<i>Shannon's the only professional
in this building.</i>

10:17.392 --> 10:18.893
<i>Friends were getting married.</i>

10:18.894 --> 10:20.978
<i>- How could I not know this?!
- Hey, guys?</i>

10:20.979 --> 10:23.230
<i>We have to deliver this episode
to the network today.</i>

10:24.399 --> 10:26.275
<i>Oh, you guys are back</i>

10:26.276 --> 10:28.444
<i>just in time for my big role.</i>

10:28.445 --> 10:30.112
<i>Hey, take it down a notch, Sarah.</i>

10:30.113 --> 10:32.490
<i>You don't even have an entry
on the Family Guy wiki.</i>

10:32.491 --> 10:35.296
<i>Even Gronk's dad has one.</i>

10:35.297 --> 10:38.322
Welcome to Old Sturbridge
Village, everyone.

10:38.323 --> 10:39.580
Here's a fun fact.

10:39.581 --> 10:43.167
In colonial times, butter
and soap were the same thing.

10:43.168 --> 10:46.504
I get that it's a fact,
but how is it fun?

10:48.465 --> 10:50.466
<i>Oh, my God!</i>

10:50.467 --> 10:52.677
<i>How the hell am I gonna get out of this?</i>

10:52.678 --> 10:54.387
<i>Shh. Nobody talk for the next minute.</i>

10:54.388 --> 10:55.763
<i>I'm about to sing my big song.</i>

10:55.764 --> 10:57.390
<i>Oh, go to hell, Peter.</i>

10:57.391 --> 10:58.933
It's no use.

10:58.934 --> 11:00.977
I guess I'm just stuck...

11:00.978 --> 11:02.979
halfway down the stairs.

11:24.210 --> 11:25.501
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

11:25.502 --> 11:27.212
<i>PETER: I'll tell you what it is:</i>

11:27.213 --> 11:29.255
<i>an homage to a classic song
from The Muppet Show,</i>

11:29.256 --> 11:31.257
<i>sung by Kermit's nephew, Robin.</i>

11:31.258 --> 11:33.009
<i>I guarantee nobody got that.</i>

11:33.010 --> 11:34.219
<i>I know this song.</i>

11:34.220 --> 11:36.012
<i>Oh, shut up, Sarah!</i>

11:41.685 --> 11:43.019
<i>I don't believe this.</i>

11:43.020 --> 11:45.188
<i>You're just singing
the same song a frog sang.</i>

11:45.189 --> 11:47.607
<i>How the hell was this
not cut from the show?</i>

11:47.608 --> 11:49.192
<i>I kind of insisted they keep it.</i>

11:49.193 --> 11:52.111
<i>I actually laid
in my parking space as a protest</i>

11:52.112 --> 11:53.696
<i>until they gave in.</i>

11:58.369 --> 12:01.829
<i>This is the stupidest
thing I've ever seen.</i>

12:01.830 --> 12:03.623
<i>Um, are they setting up</i>

12:03.624 --> 12:05.792
<i>a buffet lunch for us after this?</i>

12:05.793 --> 12:07.252
<i>No, I think it's just pizza.</i>

12:07.253 --> 12:09.504
<i>Can we please just listen to the song?</i>

12:30.776 --> 12:32.986
<i>Are there even any jokes in the song?</i>

12:32.987 --> 12:34.487
<i>Do you not understand comedy?</i>

12:34.488 --> 12:37.073
<i>It's a reference.
The joke is I'm singing it.</i>

12:37.074 --> 12:39.117
<i>Sorry to break it to
you... that's not a joke.</i>

12:39.118 --> 12:40.702
<i>Damn it, now it's over.</i>

12:40.703 --> 12:42.287
<i>Thanks a lot, Lois.
You completely ruined it.</i>

12:42.288 --> 12:44.289
<i>You better not take that tone with me,</i>

12:44.290 --> 12:46.425
<i>'cause this has been one hell of a day.</i>

12:46.426 --> 12:49.089
<i>First, I find out you make
four times what I do.</i>

12:49.090 --> 12:51.100
<i>Then I find out you were married before?</i>

12:51.101 --> 12:53.295
<i>I mean, what else don't I know?</i>

12:53.296 --> 12:54.796
<i>Well, if we're being honest, Lois,</i>

12:54.797 --> 12:57.335
<i>you're really bad at having sex
when I'm drunk.</i>

12:57.336 --> 12:58.828
<i>It's like you don't even enjoy it.</i>

12:58.829 --> 13:00.308
<i>You're impossible!</i>

13:00.309 --> 13:02.013
Do not speak to the wicked.

13:02.014 --> 13:04.494
Throw heads of cabbage at him.

13:09.477 --> 13:11.402
Damn it, Peter, this is all your fault.

13:11.403 --> 13:13.904
<i>They're not even going
to explain how we all got stuck?</i>

13:13.905 --> 13:16.805
<i>Season 16, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

13:16.806 --> 13:18.897
<i>Suddenly, the family is stuck
in the banister slats.</i>

13:18.898 --> 13:19.925
<i>Baluster.</i>

13:19.926 --> 13:21.351
<i>Brian, seriously, (BLEEP).</i>

13:21.352 --> 13:23.144
I can get us out of here.

13:23.145 --> 13:25.230
I'm good at figuring things out.

13:25.231 --> 13:26.856
Like when I figured out
the secret of business:

13:26.857 --> 13:28.858
pointing at stuff during meetings.

13:28.859 --> 13:31.320
<i>Peter, there's something you don't know.</i>

13:31.321 --> 13:33.484
<i>Chris might not even be your son.</i>

13:33.485 --> 13:34.495
What?

13:34.496 --> 13:37.184
<i>I once slept with
Philip Seymour Hoffman.</i>

13:37.185 --> 13:38.618
<i>You what?</i>

13:39.376 --> 13:41.544
<i>These montage-style cutaway gags</i>

13:41.545 --> 13:44.047
<i>provide the animators the freedom</i>

13:44.048 --> 13:45.712
<i>to go "beyond the page," as we say.</i>

13:45.713 --> 13:48.196
<i>You slept with Philip Seymour Hoffman?</i>

13:48.197 --> 13:50.021
<i>I sure did.</i>

13:50.022 --> 13:53.340
<i>It was in his trailer during
that tornado chasing movie.</i>

13:53.341 --> 13:55.827
<i>And all I know is, nine months later,</i>

13:55.828 --> 13:56.971
<i>Chris is born.</i>

13:56.972 --> 13:58.971
<i>Yay! I'm a bastard!</i>

13:58.972 --> 14:00.875
<i>This scene reminds me of the time</i>

14:00.876 --> 14:02.646
<i>I was being honored
at the Kennedy Center...</i>

14:02.647 --> 14:04.940
<i>Oh, baloney sandwich, Sarah!</i>

14:04.941 --> 14:06.595
<i>Baloney sandwich!</i>

14:06.596 --> 14:08.075
<i>In fact, you know what?!</i>

14:08.076 --> 14:09.928
<i>I'm tired of it, Peter!</i>

14:09.929 --> 14:12.780
<i>You're dishonest, you're disrespectful,</i>

14:12.781 --> 14:14.927
<i>and, frankly, I deserve better!</i>

14:14.928 --> 14:17.097
<i>So... so what are you saying, Lois?</i>

14:17.098 --> 14:20.220
<i>I'm saying this marriage is over.</i>

14:20.221 --> 14:22.816
<i>Enjoy spending the rest
of your life alone,</i>

14:22.817 --> 14:25.407
<i>and enjoy doing the show
without me, 'cause I quit!</i>

14:26.414 --> 14:28.917
building a chair with my male friends.

14:28.918 --> 14:30.213
Yeah, I can't believe...

14:30.214 --> 14:31.416
<i>Hi. Shannon Smith again.</i>

14:31.417 --> 14:34.449
<i>You know, if you need a new
Lois, I do a pretty good one.</i>

14:34.450 --> 14:36.259
<i>Peter!</i>

14:36.260 --> 14:37.568
<i>That was sad.</i>

14:38.260 --> 14:40.226
Well, that was unexpected.

14:45.786 --> 14:47.537
Well, I really regret confiscating

14:47.538 --> 14:48.947
everyone's phones now.

14:48.948 --> 14:50.710
How the hell
are we gonna get out of here?

14:50.711 --> 14:53.070
I got no idea, but we're in trouble.

14:53.071 --> 14:55.774
Even more than when we were
literally in the game Trouble.

14:55.775 --> 14:58.718
<i>Welcome back to the
DVD commentary episode.</i>

14:58.719 --> 15:01.247
If you're just joining us,
Lois has stormed out

15:01.248 --> 15:03.695
<i>and announced that she's
quitting the show after learning</i>

15:03.696 --> 15:05.952
<i>that Peter and Sarah Paulson
were once married.</i>

15:05.953 --> 15:09.184
<i>She also said Chris's dad
might be Philip Seymour Hoffman.</i>

15:09.185 --> 15:12.845
<i>More like
See-less Hoffman these days, right?</i>

15:12.846 --> 15:14.567
<i>Hey, Patrick, can we edit that out?</i>

15:14.568 --> 15:17.012
<i>- Yeah.
- Okay, good, let's do that.</i>

15:17.013 --> 15:18.436
<i>I don't see it.</i>

15:18.437 --> 15:20.260
<i>Okay, there's also a real rock</i>

15:20.261 --> 15:21.881
<i>you can throw through the glass.</i>

15:21.882 --> 15:23.337
<i>I found the fake one.</i>

15:23.338 --> 15:24.339
<i>Great.</i>

15:25.589 --> 15:27.355
Oh, thank God. Can you get us out of...

15:27.356 --> 15:29.816
Man, this is gonna be
easier than I thought.

15:31.426 --> 15:33.969
- Wait, you're robbing us?
- Sure am.

15:33.970 --> 15:36.704
And apparently,
I can take my sweet time.

15:36.705 --> 15:38.479
<i>Dad, I'm really worried about Mom.</i>

15:38.480 --> 15:39.855
<i>Should we maybe check on her?</i>

15:39.856 --> 15:42.981
<i>Or be thinking about
a paternity test for Chris?</i>

15:43.303 --> 15:45.646
<i>You're right, Meg. This is awful.</i>

15:45.647 --> 15:47.370
<i>You think your mother's actually serious</i>

15:47.371 --> 15:49.362
<i>about divorcing me
and quitting the show?</i>

15:49.363 --> 15:52.029
<i>And what was all that stuff
about Chris not being my son?</i>

15:52.030 --> 15:53.544
<i>That-that can't be true, right?</i>

15:53.545 --> 15:56.282
<i>It's a burglar party!</i>

15:56.283 --> 15:59.120
<i>Hey, remember the one day
that guy who plays the burglar</i>

15:59.121 --> 16:01.219
<i>was on set, he was passing out postcards</i>

16:01.220 --> 16:02.600
<i>for his one-man show?</i>

16:02.601 --> 16:04.806
<i>- So tacky.
- I went.</i>

16:04.807 --> 16:07.607
<i>Wasn't bad. I think I sat
next to his girlfriend,</i>

16:07.608 --> 16:09.622
<i>'cause she laughed at everything.</i>

16:12.344 --> 16:14.964
I've got a package
for a... Brian Griffin.

16:14.965 --> 16:16.550
I'm Brian Griffin.

16:16.551 --> 16:17.596
Great. Sign here.

16:17.597 --> 16:18.913
Thanks.

16:18.914 --> 16:20.690
All right, you guys.

16:20.691 --> 16:23.211
Who's ready to have some fun?

16:25.193 --> 16:26.570
Hey, Brian, they used your account

16:26.571 --> 16:28.159
to buy a karaoke machine.

16:30.348 --> 16:32.148
<i>And she said no
one would know that song.</i>

16:32.149 --> 16:33.521
<i>Well, look. The burglars know it.</i>

16:33.522 --> 16:36.200
Oh, you're kidding me.
They're doing my song.

16:40.352 --> 16:43.024
<i>I-I gotta go find your mother,
talk some sense back into her.</i>

16:43.025 --> 16:45.084
<i>No need, Peter. Hi. Sorry to interrupt.</i>

16:45.085 --> 16:46.633
<i>- Seth MacFarlane.
- Holy crap.</i>

16:46.634 --> 16:48.325
<i>It's the mouse from Sing.</i>

16:48.326 --> 16:50.051
<i>I'd recognize your voice anywhere.</i>

16:50.052 --> 16:51.251
<i>Okay, settle down.</i>

16:51.252 --> 16:53.704
<i>Mr. MacFarlane...</i>

16:53.705 --> 16:55.228
<i>what are you doing here?</i>

16:55.229 --> 16:56.292
<i>I'm actually here to tell you</i>

16:56.293 --> 16:58.249
<i>there's no need to talk sense into Lois.</i>

16:58.250 --> 16:59.882
<i>Or for a paternity test.</i>

16:59.883 --> 17:01.457
<i>Or for anyone to leave the show,</i>

17:01.458 --> 17:03.407
<i>because none of you are real.</i>

17:03.408 --> 17:05.439
<i>You're all TV characters voiced by me,</i>

17:05.440 --> 17:07.714
<i>Alex Borstein, Seth Green
and Mila Kunis.</i>

17:07.715 --> 17:08.879
<i>- Hey.
- Hey, what's up?</i>

17:08.880 --> 17:11.082
<i>- Hi, everybody.
- Wait. What?</i>

17:11.083 --> 17:12.305
<i>Okay, ha-hang on a second.</i>

17:12.306 --> 17:14.489
<i>If I'm not real,
then why does a fat nerd</i>

17:14.490 --> 17:16.563
<i>pretend to be me at every Comic-Con?</i>

17:16.564 --> 17:18.212
<i>Please, please don't mention him.</i>

17:18.213 --> 17:19.978
<i>- It'll only encourage him.
- And if you're me,</i>

17:19.979 --> 17:21.391
<i>then why do you sound like my dog?</i>

17:21.392 --> 17:23.639
<i>Because I'm also
the voice of your dog, Brian.</i>

17:23.640 --> 17:25.589
<i>Wait. You do my voice, too?</i>

17:25.590 --> 17:26.772
<i>Yeah, I do your voice.</i>

17:26.773 --> 17:29.817
<i>So, the guy who handles your money,</i>

17:29.818 --> 17:31.424
<i>he knows you by voice, right?</i>

17:31.425 --> 17:33.092
<i>That's usually just a call.</i>

17:33.093 --> 17:35.488
<i>Wait a second. If Dad's not real,</i>

17:35.489 --> 17:39.705
<i>then he's not really my dad,
which means I'm not real?</i>

17:39.706 --> 17:40.826
<i>That's right, Meg.</i>

17:40.827 --> 17:42.987
<i>You're voiced by me, Mila Kunis.</i>

17:42.988 --> 17:44.298
<i>MEG: Okay, question:</i>

17:44.299 --> 17:47.345
<i>Why is the girl who voices me
super hot and I'm not?</i>

17:47.346 --> 17:49.501
<i>Aw, that's so sweet.</i>

17:49.502 --> 17:52.589
<i>You know, believe it or not,
I've actually had two kids.</i>

17:52.590 --> 17:55.207
<i>Um, Ms. Kunis,
I would just like you to know</i>

17:55.208 --> 17:57.792
<i>that I have no problem with you
breastfeeding in this booth.</i>

17:57.793 --> 18:01.994
<i>May I ask if you're still producing?</i>

18:01.995 --> 18:05.150
<i>Uh, I, uh... no, uh, Chris,</i>

18:05.151 --> 18:07.785
<i>I'm-I'm not, uh... uh, producing.</i>

18:07.786 --> 18:09.853
<i>What about you, Miss Paulson?
Are you producing?</i>

18:09.854 --> 18:11.645
<i>I can see coming here was a mistake.</i>

18:11.646 --> 18:13.134
<i>Excuse me, Seth Green...</i>

18:13.135 --> 18:15.479
<i>Chris, I'm a man. I-I can't produce.</i>

18:15.480 --> 18:16.810
<i>Actually, I just wanted to say</i>

18:16.811 --> 18:19.963
<i>I enjoy your brilliant work
on Robot Chicken.</i>

18:19.964 --> 18:20.986
<i>Wait, Seth Green,</i>

18:20.987 --> 18:22.948
<i>are you feeding yourself
compliments now?</i>

18:22.949 --> 18:24.158
<i>Well, let's just hear Chris out.</i>

18:24.159 --> 18:25.516
<i>Okay, you know what?
We're getting off track here.</i>

18:25.517 --> 18:28.138
<i>Like I was saying,
none of you actually exists.</i>

18:28.139 --> 18:29.325
<i>Yes, you keep saying that.</i>

18:29.326 --> 18:30.918
<i>Stop telling such horrible lies.</i>

18:30.919 --> 18:32.466
<i>Oh, Seth, since you're here,</i>

18:32.467 --> 18:35.985
<i>would you mind recording
episodes 17, 14, 15, 16,</i>

18:35.986 --> 18:37.613
<i>and an NFL on Fox promo?</i>

18:37.614 --> 18:39.246
<i>Shannon, take a lap.</i>

18:39.247 --> 18:40.629
<i>Oh, hey, look.</i>

18:40.630 --> 18:42.315
<i>- Mom's back.
- Don't get excited.</i>

18:42.316 --> 18:43.666
<i>I forgot my paycheck.</i>

18:43.667 --> 18:45.286
<i>Lois, you can't leave the show.</i>

18:45.287 --> 18:46.629
<i>Oh, yeah? Why not?</i>

18:46.630 --> 18:48.207
<i>Well, the captain of the Orville says</i>

18:48.208 --> 18:50.497
<i>that none of us are real...
We're all cartoon characters.</i>

18:50.498 --> 18:53.188
<i>Not real? What-what the
hell are you talking about?</i>

18:53.189 --> 18:54.249
<i>He's right, Lois.</i>

18:54.250 --> 18:57.366
<i>Uh, my name's Alex Borstein,
and I do your voice on the show.</i>

18:57.367 --> 18:59.747
<i>Are you saying the
rough-edged comedy manager</i>

18:59.748 --> 19:02.354
<i>from The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel
does my voice?</i>

19:02.355 --> 19:04.358
<i>I'm so honored.</i>

19:04.359 --> 19:07.304
<i>I love that show. You are hilarious.</i>

19:07.305 --> 19:09.214
<i>Yeah, Seth Green already did this bit.</i>

19:09.215 --> 19:11.798
<i>So, you're really
saying that we don't exist?</i>

19:11.799 --> 19:15.207
<i>Peter, I-I'm not even sure
what this means,</i>

19:15.208 --> 19:17.917
<i>but it sure makes it seem less important</i>

19:17.918 --> 19:19.972
<i>how much money you make compared to me</i>

19:19.973 --> 19:22.055
<i>or that maybe you neglected to tell me</i>

19:22.056 --> 19:23.544
<i>everything about your past.</i>

19:23.545 --> 19:25.315
<i>Yeah, none of that stuff matters.</i>

19:25.316 --> 19:26.803
<i>You're right, Peter.</i>

19:26.804 --> 19:29.277
<i>I love you, and whatever we share,</i>

19:29.278 --> 19:30.857
<i>whether it's real or not,</i>

19:30.858 --> 19:32.684
<i>I don't want to give any of it up.</i>

19:32.685 --> 19:34.008
<i>Me, either.</i>

19:34.009 --> 19:36.997
<i>It's safe and familiar here with you.</i>

19:36.998 --> 19:41.122
<i>So let's just bury our troubles
and cling to whatever this is.</i>

19:41.123 --> 19:44.114
<i>I'm sorry I didn't tell you
about Philip Seymour Hoffman.</i>

19:44.115 --> 19:45.583
<i>It's fine. None of that matters.</i>

19:45.584 --> 19:46.776
<i>Look, the truth is...</i>

19:46.777 --> 19:48.456
<i>Again, this is Seth, not Brian...</i>

19:48.457 --> 19:50.146
<i>The truth is, you should all be thankful</i>

19:50.147 --> 19:51.393
<i>you're animated characters.</i>

19:51.394 --> 19:53.176
<i>Peter, you can drink
as much as you want,</i>

19:53.177 --> 19:54.824
<i>and nothing bad will ever happen.</i>

19:54.825 --> 19:56.376
<i>Lois, you haven't aged in decades.</i>

19:56.377 --> 19:57.866
<i>Stewie, you get to travel through time</i>

19:57.867 --> 19:59.677
<i>and do things no baby could ever do.</i>

19:59.678 --> 20:01.737
<i>And, Brian, you've had sex
with more hot women</i>

20:01.738 --> 20:04.058
<i>than a real dog
could ever reasonably expect.</i>

20:04.059 --> 20:05.705
<i>Meg, I'll admit, you got the shaft.</i>

20:05.706 --> 20:08.108
<i>Your actual life is better
than your cartoon life.</i>

20:08.109 --> 20:10.335
<i>Now, if you'll excuse me,
I need all the real actors</i>

20:10.336 --> 20:13.075
<i>to form a human shield around me
so I can get out of the building</i>

20:13.076 --> 20:15.000
<i>without the American Dad people
seeing me.</i>

20:15.001 --> 20:16.578
<i>Well, from now on, Peter,</i>

20:16.579 --> 20:18.055
<i>- I'm not going any...
- Quiet!</i>

20:18.056 --> 20:20.237
<i>My character's talking!</i>

20:20.238 --> 20:22.168
<i>Honestly, Peter, I don't know how you...</i>

20:22.169 --> 20:24.872
<i>I know. That right there
was the main reason we split up.</i>

20:24.873 --> 20:26.741
Wiped out by the German aphid,

20:26.742 --> 20:28.619
which was oddly brought by the Swedes

20:28.620 --> 20:29.964
during the Great Depression...

20:29.965 --> 20:32.172
Which, for those of you
who are too young,

20:32.173 --> 20:34.844
was like a decade-long case
of the Mondays.

20:34.845 --> 20:38.075
Well, I'm guessing you folks
are from out of town, too.

20:38.076 --> 20:41.546
<i>I never got that joke.</i>

20:48.021 --> 20:50.541
Well, you guys, I guess we all
learned something

20:50.542 --> 20:53.331
about not letting technology
rule our lives.

20:53.332 --> 20:55.993
And, Mom, next time we get
baluster slats,

20:55.994 --> 20:59.268
let's make sure there's enough
room to get our heads out.

21:01.564 --> 21:05.010
<i>Okay, thanks for watching
this outmoded form of entertainment.</i>

21:05.011 --> 21:06.429
